  "items": [
    {
      "name": "A more common habit than you'd guess",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Most adults do it",
        "occasionally, some do it",
        "several times a day",
        "",
        "It feels harmless, but it can",
        "open the door to infections"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "It can trigger nasal vestibulitis",
      "char_file": "긴장_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Picking can break the skin",
        "just inside your nostril",
        "",
        "That small injury gives",
        "bacteria an easy way in —",
        "red, swollen, tender skin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "About 30% of people carry staph in the nose",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "A large-scale nasal microbiome",
        "study (Sanger Institute/",
        "Cambridge/Imperial College London)",
        "",
        "confirmed ~30% of people",
        "carry S. aureus with",
        "no symptoms — until it",
        "enters a wound"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Why the urge keeps coming back",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Usually it's dryness",
        "",
        "When the lining dries out,",
        "mucus hardens and that",
        "crusty feeling makes you",
        "want to dig it out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Try a saline spray first",
      "char_file": "비강스프레이_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Saline loosens dried mucus",
        "with no decongestant —",
        "safe to use as often",
        "as you need"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Keep indoor humidity at 40-60%",
      "char_file": "가습기_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Especially in air-conditioned",
        "or heated rooms",
        "",
        "A humidifier keeps the lining",
        "from drying out in the first place"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "If you must, wash your hands first",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Treat allergies or a lingering",
        "cold behind the congestion",
        "",
        "Use a tissue, not a bare finger —",
        "one hand alone carries",
        "tens of thousands of bacteria"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "closing": {
    "headline": [
      [
        "A saline spray and 40-60% humidity",
        "cut the dryness that drives the urge —"
      ],
      [
        "washing your hands first",
        "cuts the infection risk when you do touch it"
      ]
    ],
    "tip": [
      "See a doctor if the area stays swollen, red, or painful for more than a couple of days",
      "Treating the underlying allergy or congestion reduces the urge more than anything else"
    ],
